\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Headline contrasts for added machinery. Each row comes from its own batch, task and recipe; rows are not comparable with each other. \texttt  {Level15} = MapFormer-WM (\texttt  {Vanilla}) plus a wrapped Kalman filter; \texttt  {Gated\_r4} = per-token sigmoid gate on the increment; hourglass = hierarchical pooling; loop = one shared layer applied four times. Estimates: accuracy difference, raw unless marked; loss-matched = at equal final training loss. Powered negative = the design could have detected the effect it dismisses; directional = consistent in sign but not detectable; take 1 / take 2 = two recipes. Reading: only recursion measurably adds more than a ceiling-level amount at training length, where the base model trains unreliably.\relax }}{8}{table.caption.26}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:machinery}{{6}{8}{Headline contrasts for added machinery. Each row comes from its own batch, task and recipe; rows are not comparable with each other. \arm {Level15} = MapFormer-WM (\arm {Vanilla}) plus a wrapped Kalman filter; \arm {Gated\_r4} = per-token sigmoid gate on the increment; hourglass = hierarchical pooling; loop = one shared layer applied four times. Estimates: accuracy difference, raw unless marked; loss-matched = at equal final training loss. Powered negative = the design could have detected the effect it dismisses; directional = consistent in sign but not detectable; take 1 / take 2 = two recipes. Reading: only recursion measurably adds more than a ceiling-level amount at training length, where the base model trains unreliably.\relax }{table.caption.26}{}}
